From 7844ec5c08512272cc3b2c04e67ca54c3ad3db82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iabdalkader <i.abdalkader@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 19:40:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] network_adapter: Do not start the station at boot.

Starting the station at boot fires WIFI_EVENT_STA_START, whose handler
calls esp_wifi_connect() with the credentials stored in flash. Every
failed attempt reconnects again from the WIFI_EVENT_STA_DISCONNECTED
handler, so a slave holding stale credentials retries forever.

Scan and disconnect requests are rejected while one of those attempts is
in flight, which leaves the host unable to scan.

Boot in WIFI_MODE_NULL, as the 0.0.5 firmware did, and leave the mode to
the host or to the scan handler, which selects one itself.

Signed-off-by: iabdalkader <i.abdalkader@gmail.com>
---
 .../esp_driver/network_adapter/main/esp_hosted_coprocessor.c    | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/esp_hosted_fg/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/esp_hosted_coprocessor.c b/esp_hosted_fg/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/esp_hosted_coprocessor.c
index 9cd0272..de63c5b 100644
--- a/esp_hosted_fg/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/esp_hosted_coprocessor.c
+++ b/esp_hosted_fg/esp/esp_driver/network_adapter/main/esp_hosted_coprocessor.c
@@ -656,7 +656,7 @@ static int connect_sta(void)
 
 	ESP_ERROR_CHECK(esp_hosted_wifi_init(&cfg));
 
-	ESP_ERROR_CHECK(esp_wifi_set_mode(WIFI_MODE_STA) );
+	ESP_ERROR_CHECK(esp_wifi_set_mode(WIFI_MODE_NULL) );
 
 #if CONFIG_WIFI_CMD_DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CN
 	/* Only set country once during first initialize wifi */
